Chapter: QuotesNoFloor

  cites Foreword chapter Console
  quotes "sha256:71f85b21050759c45724ab3a7eebe9eb36453b16b5c3878c6fdea78732bce71b" as Sorted
  trusting "fcfbf1f0f3f0f3ff" "30a23f41fc17ec2aac012d0755750484a535afbcff80882094d569bbc7bdefff" 10000

 A quotation whose chapter never declares its trust floor. The work is
 present, it hashes to its digest, it is signed, and the signer's key is
 pinned in this very source at the highest score. None of that saves it:
 the chapter never wrote 'trusting above', so it never said how much
 trust a quoted work's signer must clear, and the gate refuses to guess.
 An absent floor stamped silently as zero would be a choice made by
 omission; a declared 'trusting above 0' remains legal because it is a
 choice made out loud.

Section: Body

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
    print-line-uni ("sorted=" & show (sort-ascending 5))
  end

